{{define "title"}}{{.Heading}}{{end}}

{{define "main"}}
<section class="result-head">
  <h1>{{.Heading}}</h1>
  <dl class="birth-details">
    <div><dt>Born</dt><dd>{{.BornOn}} at {{.BornAt}}</dd></div>
    {{if .BornIn}}<div><dt>Place</dt><dd>{{.BornIn}}</dd></div>{{end}}
    <div><dt>Time zone used</dt><dd>{{.Zone}}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Universal time</dt><dd>{{.UTC}}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Houses</dt><dd>{{.System}}</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p><a class="linkish" href="/?{{.Query}}">Change these details</a></p>
</section>

{{range .Warnings}}
<div class="alert alert-warn" role="note">{{.Message}}</div>
{{end}}

{{if .Notes}}
<details class="chart-notes">
  <summary>{{len .Notes}} thing{{if ne (len .Notes) 1}}s{{end}} worth knowing about this chart</summary>
  <ul>
    {{range .Notes}}<li>{{.Message}}</li>{{end}}
  </ul>
  <p class="section-note">
    None of these is a mistake. They are the places where the chart sits on a
    boundary, and where another program may well show something slightly
    different.
  </p>
</details>
{{end}}

<section class="wheel-section">
  <h2>The chart</h2>
  <figure class="wheel-figure">
    {{.Wheel}}
    <figcaption>
      The Ascendant is on the left and the signs run anticlockwise. Solid and
      dashed lines across the middle mark the aspects between planets.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="wheel-actions">
    <button type="button" class="primary" data-download-png>Download as PNG</button>
    <button type="button" class="secondary" data-download-pdf>Download as PDF</button>
    <a class="secondary" href="/chart.svg?{{.Query}}" download="birth-chart.svg">Download as SVG</a>
    <a class="secondary" href="/chart.json?{{.Query}}">Download the data as JSON</a>
  </div>
  <p class="section-note">
    The PDF is this page as you see it &mdash; the wheel, the tables and every
    reading, laid out for paper. It comes through the browser&rsquo;s print
    dialog, so choose <em>Save as PDF</em> as the destination rather than a
    printer. The JSON file holds the same chart as data &mdash; the birth details
    as entered, every placement to six decimal places, the house cusps, the
    aspects and the readings &mdash; for loading into another program.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>The planets, the Ascendant and the Descendant</h2>
  <table class="chart-table cosmic-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Cosmic Part</th>
        <th scope="col">Zodiac sign</th>
        <th scope="col">What it defines</th>
        <th scope="col">Definition</th>
        <th scope="col">How it shows up</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range .Rows}}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row" data-label="Cosmic Part">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">{{.Glyph}}&#65038;</span>{{.CosmicPart}}
        </th>
        <td data-label="Zodiac sign">
          <span class="position">{{.Sign}}</span>
          {{if .Retrograde}}<span class="tag tag-rx" title="Retrograde">&#8478;</span>{{end}}
          <span class="tag">{{ordinal .House}} house</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="What it defines">{{.Defines}}</td>
        <td data-label="Definition">{{.Definition}}</td>
        <td data-label="How it shows up">{{.ShowsUp}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>The houses</h2>
  <p class="section-note">
    The houses divide the sky into twelve areas of life. The sign on each cusp
    colours how you approach that area.
  </p>
  <table class="chart-table houses-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">House</th>
        <th scope="col">Cusp</th>
        <th scope="col">What it governs</th>
        <th scope="col">How it shows up</th>
        <th scope="col">Planets in it</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range .Houses}}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row" data-label="House">{{ordinal .Number}}</th>
        <td data-label="Cusp"><span class="position">{{.Cusp}} {{.Sign}}</span></td>
        <td data-label="What it governs">{{.Meaning}}</td>
        <td data-label="How it shows up">{{.ShowsUp}}</td>
        <td data-label="Planets in it">{{.Occupants}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Other points</h2>
  <table class="chart-table points-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Point</th>
        <th scope="col">Zodiac sign</th>
        <th scope="col">What it defines</th>
        <th scope="col">How it shows up</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range .Points}}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row" data-label="Point">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">{{.Glyph}}&#65038;</span>{{.Name}}
        </th>
        <td data-label="Zodiac sign">
          <span class="position">{{.Sign}}</span>
          <span class="tag">{{ordinal .House}} house</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="What it defines">{{.Defines}}</td>
        <td data-label="How it shows up">{{.ShowsUp}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

{{if .Aspects}}
<section>
  <h2>Aspects</h2>
  <p class="section-note">
    Aspects are the angles planets make to one another. The orb is how far the
    angle is from exact &mdash; the smaller it is, the more strongly the pairing
    is felt.
  </p>
  <table class="chart-table aspects-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Between</th>
        <th scope="col">Aspect</th>
        <th scope="col">Orb</th>
        <th scope="col">How it shows up</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {{range .Aspects}}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row" data-label="Between">{{.Between}}</th>
        <td data-label="Aspect">
          <span class="aspect-dot aspect-{{.Family}}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">{{.Glyph}}</span>{{.Aspect}}
        </td>
        <td data-label="Orb">{{.Orb}}</td>
        <td data-label="How it shows up">{{.ShowsUp}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{end}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
{{end}}
{{end}}
